      Tiger Lily's version of this game was solvable. I want you to understand that. She built a bridge that could hold everyone if they worked together cleverly. She was proud of it. I changed one number — one tension calibration value on a bridge component that will never be visually inspected — and the solution that was correct became a trap baited with its own correctness. The most dangerous people in this game are the ones who are smart enough to find the right answer. I've simply ensured that finding the right answer is what walks them into the oscillation lock.
