    <div class="harvest-box">
      <p>The Rabbit game produces a harvest Lilly values specifically: the life-force output of people <em>actively suppressing their own vitality as a survival strategy</em>. It is a self-suppression harvest. Players are dimming themselves — cognitively, emotionally, physiologically — to survive, and the output of that deliberate diminishment feeds the ambient substrate continuously. Every minute a player spends successfully staying dim is a minute they're producing steady, controlled life-force output at a rate Lilly can harvest cleanly. It is, in her taxonomy, a slow-drip harvest as opposed to a spike harvest. Both are valuable. The Rabbit game is built for the drip.</p>
