    <div class="lilly-interlude">
      Tiger Lily put the non-strategic true detail in because she thought people deserved to be known as whole persons. I kept it because the moment someone is found — truly found, by a stranger who has known them for four days and no longer has their name — is the single most concentrated individual life-force moment I have ever measured. It is not the fear of death. It is not the grief of loss. It is the feeling of being <em>seen</em>. And it turns out that being seen, after everything has been taken, is the most powerful thing a person can feel.
    </div>

