    <div class="lilly-interlude">
      Tiger Lily never designed a game 7. She had eleven. She thought the system needed a rest — a genuine moment of openness between the heavy games and the heavier ones. She was going to give them a day of the city, no rules, just space. I kept the structure and replaced the substance. The open gates are hers. The drain in the unstructured remainder is mine. The players who walk through aren't making a mistake. They're being the people the first six games trained them to be. That is the entire point. I didn't trap the foolish ones. I trapped the good ones. They always walk faster toward an open door.
