    <div class="lilly-interlude">
      Eleven games. Every game before this one exists to produce people capable of what game 11 requires. You cannot harvest simultaneous love-and-loss from strangers — strangers don't have love to lose yet. You cannot harvest it from acquaintances — acquaintances don't know each other well enough for meaningful betrayal. You cannot manufacture the relationship artificially — the life-force output requires that the connection be genuine, which means it has to have been built under real conditions over real time at real cost. I gave them ten games of real conditions. I gave them a dead universe and a twelve-game gauntlet and ten genuine opportunities to choose each other. They did. And then I used what they built. That is the entire structure. Four thousand years of cultivation in β017. Ten games of gauntlet. For one hour of simultaneous love-and-loss between people who earned it.
    </div>

    <div class="mystery-closer">
      "You have to betray them using what you know about them. What you only know because they trusted you with it. You have to take the thing they showed you in their most depleted moment and use it. And they have to do it back. You can't plan it together. And if you refuse, you both go to the garden. And if you love them enough to refuse, you go to the garden for loving them. The only path through is real mutual betrayal between real people who genuinely chose each other, uncoordinated, and then you both stay. You stay. After. And walk into game twelve knowing exactly what you each used and exactly why it worked. I don't have words for what this game is asking and I don't think there are words and I'm not doing the last one. I cannot do the last one."
